id: pm-irviv0
title: "Registry advisories GHSA-mrwp-f3q8-3g9p (follow-redirects 1.16.1, high) and GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (minimatch 10.2.6, moderate) block the static gate on main and every PR"
description: "Both advisories were published on 2026-10-30 (22:59Z and 23:09Z). From the next CI run on main (00:02Z) and on PR #1635, the dependency advisory gate (scripts/release/dependency-advisories/gate.mjs, pm-eqxjzl) refused: the registry feed reported ids 1244003 and 1244012 while OSV was still clean, and the gate's catch-all message ('no feed success is inferred from unavailable evidence') hid the real reason, which was a non-empty registry id list. follow-redirects 1.16.1 is reached only through the CodSpeed benchmark plugin (@codspeed/vitest-plugin > @codspeed/core > axios); minimatch 10.2.6 only through eslint and @eslint/config-array. Both are development dependencies; neither establishes a CLI or SDK route. Repair: raise the pnpm override for follow-redirects to >=1.16.2 and add minimatch >=11.0.1 <12 (11.0.3 ships dual CJS/ESM exports, so eslint's require path keeps working); both releases satisfy pnpm's one-day minimum release age without an exclusion. Duplicate check: pm search for follow-redirects/minimatch/advisory returned only closed audit epics; the previous advisory repairs live under pm-qwoy (pm-dba47)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,dependencies,security
created_at: "2026-10-31T00:55:40.330Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T00:56:40.350Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T00:56:39.587Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T00:56:39.587Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
parent: pm-qwoy
resolution: "pnpm-workspace.yaml raises the follow-redirects override to >=1.16.2 <2.0.0 and adds minimatch >=11.0.1 <12.0.0; the lock now resolves follow-redirects 1.16.2 and minimatch 11.0.3 and nothing else changed. docs/DEVELOPMENT_DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md records both advisories, their development-only reach and the gate's misleading catch-all message."
expected_result: "pnpm audit and the advisory gate report zero registry and OSV ids for the locked graph; eslint and the bundle-integrity, cooldown and runtime-lock gates pass; CI Gates (static) is green again on the PR and on main."
actual_result: "node scripts/release/dependency-advisories/gate.mjs exits 0 with both feeds complete and empty id lists after the override change; pnpm lint:eslint, check-dependency-cooldown, runtime-lock check and check-development-dependencies pass locally. The hosted Gates (static) verdict is pending the PR #1635 re-run and is recorded there."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-31T00:56:15.841Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence: pnpm audit --json on the pre-repair lock listed 1244003 (follow-redirects 1.16.1, path .>@codspeed/vitest-plugin>@codspeed/core>axios>follow-redirects) and 1244012 (minimatch 10.2.6, paths via @eslint/js>eslint>@eslint/config-array and eslint directly); GitHub Dependabot had no alert for either package in any state. After raising the overrides, pnpm install changed only the two entries (follow-redirects 1.16.1 -> 1.16.2, minimatch 10.2.6 -> 11.0.3; 20 insertions, 13 deletions in pnpm-lock.yaml). node scripts/release/dependency-advisories/gate.mjs exits 0 with both feeds complete and empty id lists; pnpm lint:eslint passes with minimatch 11.0.3; check-dependency-cooldown, runtime-lock check and check-development-dependencies (CodSpeed bundle integrity) all pass. Published 2026-10-25 and 2026-10-28, both releases clear pnpm's one-day minimum release age without an exclusion; Dependabot's seven-day scheduling cooldown is unaffected."
